
This is a collection of various little ASN.1 modules, used independently
by several different testing engines below the main tree (i.e. libasn1fix)
for stressing various aspects of compiler operation.

The files follow certain naming conventions:

Source file:
	<Index>-<arbitrary-name>-{OK|SE|NP}.asn1

Regenerator test file:
	<Index>-<arbitrary-name>-{OK|SE|NP}.asn1.[<compiler-flags>]

Where
	<Index> is arbitrary number (digits)
	<arbitrary-name> is arbitrary string, without dots
	OK	file syntax and semantics are absolutely correct
	SE	file semantics is wrong
	SW	file semantics is suspicious (warning)
	NP	file syntax is incorrect, file not parseable
	<compiler-flags>	command-line flags for compiler

Example:
	07-int-OK.asn1		# Correct ASN.1 file
	07-int-OK.asn1.-EF	# Test of file regeneration with -E -F flags.

The check-parsing.sh test compares these saved outputs with the current
compiler output. Run check-parsing.sh regenerate from this directory after an
intentional output-format change, then review the resulting diff before
committing the updated fixtures. The 2026-10-23 fixture refresh records
input-wide generated-symbol indexes and earlier forward declarations for
parameterized aliases.

check-issue-592.sh compiles headers from issue-592/StructTags.asn1 and checks
that numbered parameterized instances, aliases, and prefixed types use the
defined struct tags. It also checks that a long generated tag is not truncated.

check-standard-module-order.sh creates the two standard modules in opposite
directory orders and compares the generated output. It guards against the
filesystem-dependent symbol indexes that caused PR #593 CI failures.

The 2026-11-01 BOOLEAN DEFAULT fixture refresh updates the wide-type and PER
variants of 50-constraint and the wide-type 84-param-tags output. BOOLEAN
comparison normalizes every nonzero storage value to true before comparing
with the DEFAULT. The three stale expressions caused all jobs in CI run
41362526135 to fail check-parsing.sh. This fixture-only correction preserves
the canonical omission fix, runtime validation, and every comparison check;
it introduces no production-code or input-validation change. Validate it with
make -C tests/tests-asn1c-compiler check, including the full parsing inventory.
